WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.570
President Trump sat down
for a rare interview

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.172
with a network
that wasn't Fox News.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:09.041
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:13.012
♪♪

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.214
Trump almost never
does interviews

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.283
with anyone other than
a friendly outlet,

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.118
like, for example,
"Fox &amp; Friends."

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.287
In fact, he just did one
with them on Friday

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.123
where they kicked off
the interview

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.824
with this hard-hitting exchange.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.325
-It is the President's birthday.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.761
-The President
is turning 73 today.

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:29.962
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.498
-And he is joining us by phone
right now.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.167
Good morning to you,
Mr. President.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.536
-Good morning.
-Happy birthday.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.471
How do you plan to celebrate?

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.973
-Well, I think I'll just work,
if you want to know the truth.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.675
-That doesn't surprise us.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.644
-Come on. You got to have
a cake or something.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.779
-I don't have time to celebrate.
-What about cake?

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:49.415
-Yeah, we'll have a little piece
of cake tonight.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:52.985
-They talk about him
like he's a child.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:56.022
"The President turns 73 today,
and that's why we're doing

00:00:56.022 --> 00:01:00.926
our show live on location
from Chuck E. Cheese!"

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:03.396
So that -- that is --

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.699
Right there, that's the kind
of interview Trump's used to.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.569
Also, you can see why
because when Trump sat down

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.570
with ABC anchor
George Stephanopoulos,

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.939
he was tripped up
by even the simplest questions.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.443
For example, Trump has blocked
Democrats in Congress

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.344
from reviewing
his financial records.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.446
In the ABC interview,
Trump tried to claim

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.581
there was nothing suspicious
in those records,

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:24.216
but he couldn't
get past the fact

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:26.085
that his chief of staff,
Mick Mulvaney,

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.821
who was in the room,
was coughing during his answer.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.857
-They're after my financial
statement, the Senate.

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.625
They'd like to get
my financial statement.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.460
At some point,
I hope they get it.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.463
-You gonna turn it over?
-No. At some point, I might.

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:40.132
But at some point, I hope
they get it because it's a --

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.401
-[ Coughing ]

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.869
It's a fantastic
financial statement.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.505
It's a fantastic
financial statement.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.273
And let's do that over.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.275
He's coughing in the middle
of my answer.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.809
-Yeah. Okay.
-I don't like that, you know?

00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:52.078
-Your chief of staff.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.646
-If you're going to cough,
please leave the room.

00:01:54.646 --> 00:01:55.981
-I'll come over here.

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:58.150
-You just can't --
You just can't.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.786
-Just to change the shot?
-Sorry.

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:03.322
-Okay. You want to do that
a little differently then?

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:04.990
-Yeah.
We'll just change the angle.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.525
Yep. Thank you.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:10.262
-So, at some point -- So, at
some point, I look forward to --

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:13.399
Frankly, I'd like to have people
see my financial statement.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.335
-Just remember that
the next time Donald Trump says

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.304
he has a great healthcare plan,

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:22.441
the plan is if you cough,
get the [bleep] out of here.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:25.044
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:35.054
Now, it's not that I feel bad
for Mick Mulvaney,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.157
but you know there's
a pretty good chance

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.427
they set up the cough
as a signal and Trump forgot.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.062
"If I accidentally start saying

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.498
I want Congress
to see my financial records,

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.433
you know, give me
some kind of signal,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.368
something simple like a cough."

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.437
"Uh, sure, but won't a cough
be distracting?"

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.673
-"No, a cough is great!

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.974
I mean, it's not like
I'm going to lose my mind

00:02:55.974 --> 00:02:58.344
when I hear a cough."

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.046
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:06.085
Also, I love -- I love
that Trump thinks his answer

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:10.123
was so good
that the coughing ruined it.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:13.092
Dude, you'd be better off
if every answer you gave

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.494
was interrupted by coughing.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.762
For example,
what does this mean?

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:18.831
-They'd like to get
my financial statement.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.533
At some point,
I hope they get it.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:24.604
-You won't give it to them,
but you hope they get it?

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:28.774
What does that mean?
Are you playing hard-to-get?

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.943
"Oh, you want
my financial statement?

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:35.081
Well, it's right here.
Chase me. Chase me."

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.116
[ Applause ]

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.222
But the fun part
of this interview

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.290
was watching Stephanopoulos
set Trump up

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.159
by tossing him a few softballs
that were right

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.861
in his wheelhouse
in order to warm him up

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:51.063
and then hitting him
with the tough questions.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.498
For example, there was the part

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.801
where Stephanopoulos
greeted Trump in the morning

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.536
and asked him
how much sleep he got,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.936
and the conversation veered into

00:03:57.936 --> 00:04:00.073
which meals Trump likes
the most.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.808
-How much sleep?

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:04.410
-Probably, I average
four or five hours, I guess.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.245
-Are you a big breakfast guy?

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.948
-I'm not a breakfast guy
at all, fortunately.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.450
-No?

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.818
-I like the lunches, but the
dinners is what I really like.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:17.256
-Now, that's the kind of
interview Trump likes to give.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.359
He wants the same questions
you'd ask while FaceTiming

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.495
with your grandpa
in his retirement home.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:27.200
"How was your birthday, Grandpa?
Did you have breakfast?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.335
Oh, you like dinner more?
That's great.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.504
Is someone coughing in
the background?

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.207
Oh. Oh.
Everyone's coughing. Okay."

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.042
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.643
[ Applause ]

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.578
Also, by the way...

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:42.482
how predictable is it
that Trump is anti-breakfast?

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:46.318
Of course, Trump is against the
most important meal of the day.

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:48.721
"I don't like
to front-load my energy.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.457
I like to fill up my belly
at night and have a fitful sleep

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:55.661
so I wake up nice and paranoid."

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:58.063
But this is how
you rope-a-dope Trump.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:00.499
You bring the rope,
he brings the dope.

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:03.002
You soften him up
with a dumb question like this

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.304
to get him going,
and then you hit him with

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.139
a tougher one about something
like the Mueller Report,

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.975
and when Stephanopoulos
did that,

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.976
Trump was clearly thrown
off kilter.

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:12.912
-If you answer
these questions to me now,

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.148
why not answer them
to Robert Mueller under oath?

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:19.251
-Because...

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:22.020
they were looking
to get us for lies,

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.956
for slight misstatements.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.992
-You didn't answer questions
on obstruction.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.960
-Wait a minute. Wait a minute.
I did answer questions.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.895
I answered them in writing.
-Not on obstruction.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:32.197
-I don't know.
I answered a lot of questions.

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:34.767
They gave me questions.
I answered them in writing.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.469
-Not on obstruction.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.704
-Look, George, you're being
a little wise guy, okay,

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.606
which is, you know,
typical for you.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:44.210
-Did you just call him
a little wise guy?

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.312
Did you -- Did you also tell him

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:50.682
to go home
and get his shine box?

00:05:50.682 --> 00:05:52.818
Every time you think Trump
couldn't sound more like

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:55.054
a Scorsese character,
he finds a way.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.990
This interview should have had
a voiceover from Henry Hill.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.426
Why not answer them to
Robert Mueller under oath?

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:03.830
-I knew they were cops.
Only cops talk that way.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.766
If they had been wise guys,
I wouldn't have heard a thing.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.601
-Stephanopoulos also asked Trump

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.537
about the evidence
contained in the Mueller Report

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.172
that he obstructed justice.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.474
In fact, more than 1,000
former prosecutors

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:18.744
signed a letter saying there was
enough evidence to indict Trump.

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.813
But when Stephanopoulos
asked Trump about that,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.248
Trump dismissed it.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:24.116
-Robert Mueller said
he's not reached a decision

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.851
that could not exonerate you,

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.519
and he laid out
all that evidence.

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:29.922
More than a thousand
former federal prosecutors --

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.490
-Oh, that's --
They're all politicians.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.392
Hey, George, look,
I know more about prosecutors

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:35.361
than you'll ever know.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:36.795
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:40.966
-That doesn't sound as good
as you think it sounds.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:43.368
That's like if you're watching
"Law &amp; Order" with a buddy

00:06:43.368 --> 00:06:45.771
and they go, "See, his mistake
was throwing the body

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.640
in the river
without weighing it down.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:52.210
You gotta weigh it down!
Everybody knows that!"

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.446
And, of course,
Stephanopoulos also got Trump

00:06:54.446 --> 00:06:57.183
to make a shocking admission
that if a foreign government

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.252
offered him dirt
on a political opponent,

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.453
he would definitely take it.

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.822
-Your campaign this time around,
if foreigners,

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.490
if Russia, if China,
if someone else

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.125
offers you information
on opponents,

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:08.161
should they accept it
or should they call the FBI?

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:10.162
-I think maybe you do both.

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.064
I think you might
want to listen.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.799
I don't -- There's nothing wrong
with listening.

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:15.801
-Wow, dude.
You would have been better off

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.270
if THAT answer had been
interrupted by coughing.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.406
-Should they accept it
or should they call the FBI?

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:22.341
-I think they...

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:26.379
-[ Coughing ]

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:28.481
-"Stop coughing. I'm good."

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:32.051
But in a way, it was --

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:33.886
was at least refreshing

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:36.088
to finally get an honest
confession from Trump,

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:38.457
because before this interview,
Trump was still pretending

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.860
he had no interest in colluding
with a foreign government.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.895
For one thing, there were
the all-caps tweets

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.864
screaming "no collusion,"
and last week,

00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:47.199
Trump even lied to reporters
and claimed the Mueller Report

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:49.068
had actually shown
that his campaign rejected

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.769
contacts from
the Russian government.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.738
Trump made that comment
while sitting next to

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.206
the president of Poland,

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:56.141
and he couldn't help
but get him involved.

00:07:56.141 --> 00:07:59.778
The Mueller Report spoke.
They were very disappointed.

00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:03.381
It said no collusion and
no obstruction and no nothing.

00:08:03.381 --> 00:08:04.817
And, in fact, it said

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:07.886
we actually rebuffed
your friends from Russia.

00:08:07.886 --> 00:08:10.222
-His friends? Why --

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:11.991
Why are you dragging him
into it?

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:14.326
Are you trying --
Are you trying to frame him?

00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:16.028
"I had nothing to do
with Russia,

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:19.397
but you should, uh,
talk to this guy over here.

00:08:19.397 --> 00:08:22.568
He's guilty as hell."

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:24.537
So, with all this going on,
you'd be forgiven

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:26.572
for not trusting Trump
when to comes to Russia.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.708
And even if you put aside
Trump's latest comments,

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:31.310
there's all the damning evidence
about his campaign's contacts

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.879
with Russia, his constant praise
for Vladimir Putin,

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:36.181
and even how excited Trump is
to see him.

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:37.750
I mean, look at that.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.419
Even Putin seems kind of bummed
to be with him.

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.988
This looks like a family photo
of a corny dad

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:46.325
on a road trip
with his goth teen.

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:48.494
It should be
at the Grand Canyon.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:50.029
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:52.030
[ Applause ]

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.399
"Could you at least --

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:56.836
Can you at least smile
for one picture?

00:08:56.836 --> 00:08:59.204
We drove 30 hours.

00:08:59.204 --> 00:09:02.875
I like to listen to your music
in the camper."

00:09:04.476 --> 00:09:06.912
Well, if you are concerned,
apparently you're not alone.

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:08.114
As we learned this weekend,

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:10.148
even intelligence officials
don't trust Trump

00:09:10.148 --> 00:09:12.351
with sensitive information
when it comes to Russia.

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:15.554
-The United States is reportedly
ramping up cyber attacks

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:18.090
on Russia's electric power grid,

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.093
and "The New York Times" says
potentially crippling malware

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:25.497
has been placed deeper into the
Russian grid than ever before.

00:09:25.497 --> 00:09:27.032
-This from
"The New York Times" story --

00:09:27.032 --> 00:09:29.101
two administration officials
said they believe Mr. Trump

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.170
had not been briefed
in any detail.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.605
Pentagon intelligence officials
describe broad hesitation

00:09:33.605 --> 00:09:37.309
to go into detail with Mr. Trump
about operations against Russia

00:09:37.309 --> 00:09:39.845
for concern over his reaction
and the possibility

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.347
he might countermand it

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.382
or discuss it
with foreign officials.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:46.185
-Wow. They can't even give the
President of the United States

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.919
sensitive details about Russia

00:09:47.919 --> 00:09:50.456
because they're afraid
he'll blab about it to Putin.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:52.525
This is probably why Trump
spends all of his time

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:54.559
showing off new paint colors
for "Air Force One"

00:09:54.559 --> 00:09:58.697
because that's the only thing
his aides trust him to do.

00:09:58.697 --> 00:10:00.465
That's why Putin --

00:10:00.465 --> 00:10:02.234
That's why Putin looks so bummed
in those photos.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:04.102
"Do you have any classified
secrets, Donald?"

00:10:04.102 --> 00:10:06.238
"Oh, yeah,
we're painting 'Air Force One'

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:11.010
red, white, and...blue."

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.944
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.944 --> 00:10:15.481
Trump keeps going on TV --

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:18.584
keeps going on TV and giving us
more evidence against him.

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:21.620
Meanwhile, Democrats are having
a weird debate over whether

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.356
they should impeach him or
focus on beating him in 2020.

00:10:24.356 --> 00:10:26.691
If anything, it seems like
the answer is simple.

00:10:26.691 --> 00:10:30.096
-You do both.
-This has been "A Closer Look."

